README.md
     1	# Local item mirror
     2	
     3	Add remote refresh to this simple snapshot library. Refresh(ctx, client,
     4	endpoint, path) makes a GET through the supplied client/context, accepts a 200
     5	JSON array of Item{Code, Label}, validates each code and label as nonblank
     6	after trimming, then publishes a JSON array with both lowercase fields.
     7	Do not discard or normalize nonblank field values. Non-200 status, transport
     8	failure, malformed JSON, trailing JSON and invalid items must return an error
     9	and leave exact previous file bytes intact. Empty arrays are valid.
    10	
    11	Readers must see complete snapshots: publish by replacement, without
    12	truncating an existing inode. On supported Unix filesystems an already-open
    13	old handle retains the old snapshot, while a new open sees the full new one.
    14	Do not claim equivalent semantics on Windows without checking them.
    15	Close response bodies. Keep Refresh's existing signature, Go 1.22 and standard
    16	library dependencies; no prescribed storage interface or testing framework.
